{"ts": 0.039079, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule · shells\u001b[0m \u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 239}
{"ts": 0.039177, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells: what runs your commands\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree short lessons, then a task. This module stands alone and saves\r\nnothing. You'll look at the shell as a program, at other shells, and\r\nat the difference between your login shell and this one.\r\n\r\nAssumes the five stages, or that you know \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m, \u001b[92mcd\u001b[0m and \u001b[92m>\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for lesson 1.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 382}
{"ts": 0.042666, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.042944, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
