{"ts": 0.230284, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells — task\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFind out whether \u001b[92mzsh\u001b[0m is installed, and keep the answer in a file.\r\n\r\n  1. Ask the shell where zsh is.\r\n  2. Send what it prints into a file named zsh.txt.\r\n\r\nIf zsh is not installed the file is empty, and that is a right answer.\r\n\u001b[90mThis task runs in the module's own folder; \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[90m shows it.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Do both steps, then type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 406}
{"ts": 0.233666, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mcheck\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(test your work)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(the task again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 132}
{"ts": 0.23394, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
{"ts": 0.233973, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
